      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART I, LINE 32B:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>AS SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION'S DONOR-ENGAGEMENT TEAM INTERACTS WITH DONORS INTENDING TO GIVE CURRENT OR FUTURE (PLANNED) GIFTS, IF THE TRANSACTION INVOLVES REAL ESTATE, THE DEVELOPMENT OFFICER REFERS THE TRANSACTION TO THE SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION'S CFO TO BRING TO THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION'S BOARD. IF THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION ACCEPTS THE PROPERTY, THE DONATION IS MADE DIRECTLY TO THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION TO HOLD, MANAGE, AND MARKET THE REAL ESTATE. WHEN THE PROPERTY IS SOLD, NET PROCEEDS ARE GRANTED TO SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION TO BE APPLIED TO THE DONOR'S INTENDED CHARITABLE PURPOSE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleM>
    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="RetDoc1044400001">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART IV, LINE 12B:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION IS A SUPPORTING ORGANIZATION OF SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION. THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS OF THE SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION AND ALL SUPPORTING ORGANIZATIONS, INCLUDING THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION, ARE AUDITED ON A CONSOLIDATED BASIS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION A, LINE 6</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION HAS ONE CLASS OF VOTING MEMBERS CONSISTING OF THE BOARD OF GOVERNORS OF ITS SUPPORTED ORGANIZATION, SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION. APPROVAL OF THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION'S DIRECTORS IS CONSIDERED AND APPROVED BY THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION'S BOARD OF DIRECTORS. TWO MEMBERS OF THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION'S BOARD OF DIRECTORS MUST ALSO BE MEMBERS OF THE BOARD OF GOVERNORS OF ITS SUPPORTED ORGANIZATION, SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION, AND THE PRESIDENT AND CEO IS A MEMBER OF THE BOARD.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION A, LINE 8B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ONLY COMMITTEE FOR SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION IS THE BOARD. THERE IS NO OTHER COMMITTEE WITH AUTHORITY TO ACT ON BEHALF OF THE GOVERNING BODY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>FORM 990 IS REVIEWED BY THE CFO OF SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION, WHO IS THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION'S TREASURER, FOR ACCURACY AND COMPLETENESS. A COMPLETE COPY OF FORM 990 WAS PROVIDED TO SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION'S AUDIT COMMITTEE AND BOARD OF GOVERNORS FOR THEIR REVIEW BEFORE THE RETURN WAS FILED WITH THE INTERNAL REVENUE SERVICE.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY IS SIGNED BY EACH BOARD MEMBER AT THE ANNUAL MEETING OF THE BOARD. AT EACH SUBSEQUENT BOARD MEETING, THE CHAIR ASKS EACH BOARD MEMBER TO DISCLOSE ANY NEW CONFLICTS. ANY DISCLOSURES ARE NOTED IN THE MINUTES OF THAT MEETING. IF A TRANSACTION ARISES WHERE THERE IS A CONFLICT OF INTEREST, THE PERSON WITH SUCH CONFLICT IS NOT ALLOWED TO VOTE ON THE TRANSACTION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE BYLAWS, ARTICLES OF INCORPORATION, IRS DETERMINATION LETTER, AND THE CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY ARE AVAILABLE TO THE PUBLIC BY CONTACTING THE SUPPORTED ORGANIZATION, SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION. THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS ARE REPORTED ON A CONSOLIDATED BASIS AND ARE AVAILABLE ON SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION'S WEBSITE, WWW.SDFOUNDATION.ORG.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART XII, LINE 2C:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION IS A SUPPORTING ORGANIZATION OF SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION. THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS OF THE SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION AND ALL SUPPORTING ORGANIZATIONS, INCLUDING THE SAN DIEGO CHARITABLE REAL ESTATE FOUNDATION, ARE AUDITED ON A CONSOLIDATED BASIS. SAN DIEGO FOUNDATION HAS AN AUDIT COMMITTEE WHICH IS CHARGED WITH THE RESPONSIBILITY OF OVERSIGHT OF THE AUDIT AND ITS FINANCIAL STATEMENTS AND SECTION OF AN INDEPENDENT ACCOUNTANT.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
